# What EAS Build leaves out of the upload (plan 17).
#
# EAS archives this monorepo by copying the folder and, without this file,
# applying only the ROOT .gitignore. The nested ones (apps/web, apps/native,
# apps/server, packages/*) aren't read, so their build output went up with
# every Android build: apps/web/.next alone is 167 MB. With this file present,
# EAS ignores .gitignore entirely and uses only these rules. Anything the
# .gitignore files keep out must also be listed here, secrets above all.
#
# What must stay: every workspace package's source and package.json,
# pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml and .npmrc. EAS runs `pnpm install` on the
# whole workspace, and packages/db's postinstall generates its client from
# prisma/.

# ── Secrets, never uploaded ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# ── Dependencies and caches (EAS installs its own) ─────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.turbo/
.cache/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# ── Build output, from every app and package ───────────────────────────
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.expo/
web-build/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
.vercel/
.alchemy/
.wrangler/
.open-next/
packages/db/prisma/generated/
apps/server/server

# ── The native projects: EAS generates them from app.json (prebuild) ───
apps/native/android/
apps/native/ios/
apps/native/.kotlin/

# ── Not needed to build the app ────────────────────────────────────────
designs/
plans/
systems/
progress/
.claude/
*.tgz
tmp/
temp/
